statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-3,4]$\n- ${∬}_{R}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-4,4]\\times [-2,2]$" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407327 1072 #uuid "04b43074-9710-54c1-a656-7d7797008d68" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407327 1074 "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407326 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1069 "q-129908" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1071 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-1$ and $y=2-|x|.$ If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n- ${\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1072 #uuid "bbe5a871-1924-5655-ad62-5cf32208bd34" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407328 1074 "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/1a/1a5369b58b14444c5ea0ce4bb36954d1d0b7964dcef4e95f9cc527694b3a9e4f.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- Functions I and III equal $x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ on $D$ and equal $0$ outside $D.$\n\n- We cannot use function II. The function is not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(1,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the function is nonzero at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407324 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1069 "q-86866" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1071 "![](images/51/51706be38cc1c72079fe702c899b575ea53ba4d85e7990a6aa81f20dc8da4de3.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [0,3]$\n- ${∬}_{R}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-5,5]\\times [0,3]$\n- ${∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1072 #uuid "ed965e5b-f0df-5c0f-9c7c-0cb7a433c067" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407329 1074 "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}(y{x}^{2}+3x{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407330 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407333 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407330 1062 #uuid "080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407330 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152833 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407331 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407334 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407331 1062 #uuid "30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407331 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407327 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407332 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407330 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407332 1062 #uuid "4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407332 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152832 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407333 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407331 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407333 1062 #uuid "5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407333 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407329 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407334 1062 #uuid "98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb" 13194139533539 17592186045585 true] [17592186407334 1063 #edb/r